WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:05.300
Hey there, welcome to your second drink of beach games.
嘿，欢迎来到你们的第二杯“海滩游戏”。

2
00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.040
Lady, did you know that this episode was originally titled Coal Walk?
女士，你知道这一集最初的标题是《煤炭行走》吗？

3
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:11.320
Coal Walk?
《煤炭行走》？

4
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:11.920
I didn't.
我不知道。

5
00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:15.560
Yeah, that's just one of the little extra tidbits I uncovered.
是啊，这只是我挖掘出的小花絮之一。

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:21.260
I found the original pitch document for this episode, and that's what it was called.
我找到了这一集的原始提案文件，上面就是这么写的。

7
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.980
I also went into our mailbag, and we got some fun letters about this one.
我还翻看了我们的信箱，收到了一些关于这一集的有趣来信。

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.160
I like it.
我喜欢这个。

9
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.240
I have a couple of fun candy bag talking heads I want to share,
我有几个有趣的“糖果袋”采访片段想分享，

10
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.880
and the first one is right at the top of the episode.
第一个就在这一集的开头。

11
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:39.140
Meredith has a talking head where she is talking about her wearing a bathing suit to work,
梅雷迪思有个采访片段，她在说自己穿泳装上班的事，

12
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.420
and she ends up flashing the camera.
结果她最后对着镜头走光了。

13
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.440
Yes, I remember because you made a flash count.
没错，我记得，因为你还专门数了她走光的次数。

14
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.840
Well, there was an alt that I thought was great.
嗯，还有一个备选片段我觉得很棒。

15
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:55.080
Meredith says, I grew up at the beach, and by grew up, I mean got drunk and lost my virginity behind a pile of rocks.
梅雷迪思说：“我在海边长大，所谓的长大，就是喝得烂醉，还在一堆石头后面丢了初夜。”

16
00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.040
Oh my goodness.
天哪。

17
00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.160
Meredith isn't the only person who was going to share about having sex at the beach.
梅雷迪思并不是唯一一个分享在海边发生性关系的人。

18
00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:03.540
This was a theme.
这成了一个主题。

19
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:09.860
Ryan had a talking head where he said, great, we're going to the one place I had sex with Kelly outside,
瑞安有个采访片段，他说：“太棒了，我们要去那个我曾和凯莉在户外发生过关系的地方，

20
00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.300
and I just know she won't be able to keep her mouth shut.
而且我知道她肯定管不住自己的嘴。”

21
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:13.620
Thanks a lot, Michael.
真是太感谢你了，迈克尔。

22
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.460
You couldn't take us to the movies?
你就不能带我们去看电影吗？

23
00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:16.780
Oh, wait.
哦，等等。

24
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.140
That wouldn't work either.
那也不行。

25
00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:26.390
And finally, there was a Phyllis talking head that gave us more insight into her relationship with Bob.
最后，还有一个菲利斯的采访片段，让我们更深入地了解了她和鲍勃的关系。

26
00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:30.250
Phyllis says, I'm excited to go to the lake.
菲利斯说：“我很兴奋能去湖边。”

27
00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.430
I just hope Michael doesn't make us swim.
我只希望迈克尔别逼我们游泳。

28
00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.150
Bob doesn't like it when I shave my legs.
鲍勃不喜欢我刮腿毛。

29
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.610
Oh my God!
天哪！

30
00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:37.730
What?
怎么了？

31
00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.150
That Beach Games candy bag was so provocative.
那个“海滩游戏”的糖果袋内容太劲爆了。

32
00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:41.990
I know.
我知道。

33
00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:44.630
What was up with the writers that week?
编剧们那周是怎么了？

34
00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:55.330
Well, I watched the super fan of this episode, and there are a lot of fun added tidbits, and I wanted to talk about three.
嗯，我看了这一集的超级粉丝版，里面增加了很多有趣的细节，我想聊聊其中三个。

35
00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:56.150
Okay.
好的。

36
00:01:56.630 --> 00:02:01.550
First of all, at the top of the episode, as everyone is talking about getting ready for the beach,
首先，在这一集的开头，当大家都在谈论准备去海滩时，

37
00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:08.170
you see Kelly and Ryan back in the annex, and Kelly is trying to pick a bathing suit.
你可以看到凯莉和瑞安在附楼里，凯莉正在挑泳衣。

38
00:02:08.390 --> 00:02:08.730
Okay.
好的。

39
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:17.190
So, she's sitting on the ground, and she's got these two bathing suits in front of her, and I'll let you hear it.
她坐在地上，面前放着两件泳衣，我让你听听这段。

40
00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:17.470
Okay.
好的。

41
00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:21.570
Why is this so crazy hard?
为什么这事儿这么难啊？

42
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.710
Ryan, how do you make decisions?
瑞安，你是怎么做决定的？

43
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:28.110
I realize that no matter what decision I make, it won't change the course of anything,
我意识到无论我做什么决定，都不会改变任何事情的走向，

44
00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.170
and I shouldn't have bothered anyone by saying it out loud.
而且我不该把它说出来去打扰别人。

45
00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:34.710
Well, that is so not the case with us, Ryan.
好吧，瑞安，我们之间可不是这样。

46
00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:39.130
And this is, like, the hardest decision I've ever had to make in my whole life.
这简直是我这辈子做过最难的决定了。

47
00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:41.110
Ryan is so over it.
瑞安真是受够了。

48
00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:41.490
Oh.
哦。

49
00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.410
He's like, I tell myself that this makes no difference.
他就像是在说，我告诉自己这根本没区别。

50
00:02:46.570 --> 00:02:47.250
All right.
好吧。

51
00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:54.390
And then there was this little bit that was added back to the top of the scene where Michael approaches Pam.
还有这一小段被加回到了迈克尔走向帕姆那场戏的开头。

52
00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:59.630
You know, this is where he's going to tell her that she has to take diligent notes at the beach.
你知道，这是他要告诉她，在海滩上必须认真做笔记的地方。

53
00:02:59.830 --> 00:03:00.050
Right.
没错。

54
00:03:00.050 --> 00:03:05.650
Well, this part that they added back gives you a glimpse into her situation with Roy.
嗯，他们加回来的这一部分让你得以一窥她和罗伊之间的情况。

55
00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:06.210
Oh.
哦。

56
00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:11.850
Which I thought was kind of cool, considering that we know what's going to happen later with, you know.
我觉得这挺酷的，考虑到我们都知道后来会发生什么，你知道的。

57
00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:12.650
The cold walk.
那场冷战。

58
00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.090
Yeah.
是啊。

59
00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.850
So, here it is.
所以，就是这里。

60
00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:19.710
Pam, you broke up with your boyfriend and then kept working together.
帕姆，你和男朋友分手了，然后还继续在一起工作。

61
00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:20.870
How did that work out?
那情况怎么样？

62
00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:25.810
You remember you fired Roy for attacking Jim, and I don't talk to him anymore, really.
你记得你因为罗伊袭击吉姆而解雇了他，而且我真的不再和他说话了。

63
00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:26.790
Hmm.
嗯。

64
00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:28.550
Acrimonious.
关系很僵啊。

65
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:28.670
Yes.
是的。

66
00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:29.510
Yeah.
是啊。

67
00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.490
She reveals, I don't talk to him anymore.
她透露说，我不再和他说话了。

68
00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:33.430
Yeah.
是啊。

69
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.030
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

70
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.190
Pretty clean break, it sounds like.
听起来分得很彻底。

71
00:03:36.410 --> 00:03:36.670
Yeah.
是啊。

72
00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:39.930
Well, finally, we got a letter from Emily L., who said,
好了，最后，我们收到了一封来自艾米丽·L的信，她说，

73
00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:47.190
In Beach Games, when they're all sitting down and Michael announces a hot dog eating contest, Phyllis asks for mustard.
在《海滩游戏》里，当大家坐下来，迈克尔宣布要举行热狗大赛时，菲利斯要了芥末酱。

74
00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:52.030
Michael says, no mustard, just dip it in water so it'll slide down your gullet more easily.
迈克尔说，没有芥末酱，蘸点水，这样更容易滑进你的食道。

75
00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.330
And no one says anything after this.
说完之后没人接话。

76
00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.350
Phyllis and Angela just look at each other.
菲利斯和安吉拉只是互相看了看。

77
00:03:56.350 --> 00:04:03.250
But in season six, episode 14, the banker, remember, this was our clip show.
但在第六季第14集《银行家》里，记得吗，那是我们的剪辑集。

78
00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:03.810
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

79
00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:09.050
Toby and the banker are talking, and they're talking about all these old scenes, and they're replaying them.
托比和银行家在聊天，他们谈论着所有这些旧场景，并且在重播它们。

80
00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:19.350
The hot dog scene replays, Phyllis asks for the mustard, Michael tells her to dip it in water so it'll slide down her gullet more easily, and then everyone says,
热狗那场戏重播了，菲利斯要了芥末酱，迈克尔让她蘸点水，这样更容易滑进她的食道，然后每个人都说，

81
00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.510
that's what she said, and laughs, and Michael gets mad.
那是她说的，然后大笑，迈克尔很生气。

82
00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.150
Emily L.
艾米丽·L

83
00:04:24.350 --> 00:04:26.810
said, why are these two scenes different?
说，为什么这两个场景不一样？

84
00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:35.570
Well, Angela, you talked about this moment in our breakdown, that this was in the deleted scenes, this big, that's what she said moment.
嗯，安吉拉，你在我们的解析中谈到过这个时刻，这是在删减片段里的，这个巨大的“那是她说的”时刻。

85
00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:38.470
It has been added back to the Peacock superfan.
它已经被加回到了Peacock的超级粉丝版里。

86
00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:44.650
In fact, there is so much added back to this hot dog eating contest moment.
事实上，这个热狗大赛的片段里加回了太多内容。

87
00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.910
You get to see the scene of Pam making the hot dogs.
你可以看到帕姆制作热狗的场景。

88
00:04:48.070 --> 00:04:53.210
You get to see Michael getting so annoyed that people won't eat the hot dogs.
你可以看到迈克尔因为大家不吃热狗而变得非常恼火。

89
00:04:53.390 --> 00:04:54.910
It's so much longer.
它长多了。

90
00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.410
And when I was watching it, it just took me back.
当我观看的时候，它瞬间把我带回了过去。

91
00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.830
I remember shooting it.
我记得拍摄的时候。

92
00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:00.490
It was so funny.
太搞笑了。

93
00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:06.310
I just love when, like, Michael gets annoyed at us.
我就是喜欢迈克尔对我们感到恼火的样子。

94
00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:06.650
Yeah.
是啊。

95
00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:09.370
It's, like, such a funny dynamic.
这真是一种有趣的互动。

96
00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:12.390
It's like father with a bunch of, like, toddlers.
就像父亲带着一群蹒跚学步的孩子。

97
00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:12.690
Yes.
没错。

98
00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:13.550
Like, his energy.
就像他的那种劲头。

99
00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:14.570
That's exactly it.
完全就是这样。

100
00:05:14.570 --> 00:05:16.930
Like, no one wants to put their shoes on.
就像没人愿意穿上他们的鞋子一样。

101
00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:22.730
No one wants to put on the hat, and it's cold out, and he's just, like, trying to wrangle a bunch of cats.
没人想戴那顶帽子，外面又冷，他就像是在试图管教一群猫一样。

102
00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:29.470
Yeah, it's definitely, if you have Peacock, this is a superfan episode, I think, not to be missed.
没错，如果你有Peacock平台，这绝对是一集超级粉丝特辑，我觉得不容错过。

103
00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:34.950
But finally, Angela, we got this letter that I just had to share from Katie S.
但最后，安吉拉，我们收到了一封我必须分享的信，来自凯蒂·S。

104
00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.430
You're not going to believe this.
你绝对不敢相信。

105
00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:37.410
Here's what Katie said.
凯蒂是这么说的。

106
00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:42.090
I just want to say I do think your podcast is cursed, but it's okay.
我只想说，我确实觉得你们的播客被诅咒了，但没关系。

107
00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:43.430
I will keep listening.
我会继续收听的。

108
00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:47.870
Thankfully, during the bird funeral episode, I did not see any dead birds.
谢天谢地，在鸟儿葬礼那一集，我没有看到任何死鸟。

109
00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.910
Thankfully, because so many people did.
谢天谢地，因为很多人都看到了。

110
00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.290
And it just keeps going on and on.
而且这事儿还没完没了。

111
00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:54.070
We're still getting mail about it.
我们还在收到关于那件事的邮件。

112
00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:54.570
I know.
我知道。

113
00:05:54.570 --> 00:06:00.310
But while listening to beach games, I was walking on a walking trail in the woods,
但在听《海滩游戏》那一集时，我正走在树林里的步道上，

114
00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:08.830
and during the part where you mentioned how Leslie had to go to the hospital because rain accidentally kicked sand in his eye,
就在你们提到莱斯利因为雷不小心把沙子踢进他眼睛里而不得不去医院的那一段时，

115
00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:17.370
something, Katie says, either a fly or a large piece of dirt, flew in my eye.
凯蒂说，有什么东西，要么是一只苍蝇，要么是一大块泥土，飞进了我的眼睛里。

116
00:06:17.510 --> 00:06:18.050
No.
不会吧。

117
00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:18.710
Yes.
真的。

118
00:06:19.250 --> 00:06:21.410
Katie said it was one of those scary times.
凯蒂说那是相当吓人的一次经历。

119
00:06:21.550 --> 00:06:25.290
You could see it coming, but it just happened so fast you can't do anything.
你能预见到它要飞过来，但发生得太快了，你什么也做不了。

120
00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.110
I very thankfully did not have to go to the doctor.
万幸的是，我没必要去看医生。

121
00:06:28.390 --> 00:06:30.430
I'm unsure if my cornea was scratched.
我不确定我的角膜有没有被划伤。

122
00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:32.930
I'm guessing maybe slightly, but was able to heal.
我猜可能有一点，但已经自愈了。

123
00:06:33.110 --> 00:06:36.150
I was in absolute searing pain that lasted a couple days.
我当时感到剧痛无比，持续了好几天。

124
00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:39.730
It's gotten much better, but I just thought that was the craziest thing.
现在好多了，但我只是觉得这事儿太疯狂了。

125
00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:40.770
That is.
确实是。

126
00:06:40.770 --> 00:06:48.290
Can you imagine listening to a story about someone getting something in their eye, and then you get something in your eye at that same moment?
你能想象吗？听着关于别人眼睛进东西的故事，结果就在那一瞬间，你的眼睛也进东西了？

127
00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:48.670
At the same time?
就在同一时间？

128
00:06:49.110 --> 00:06:50.290
That's so trippy.
这太诡异了。

129
00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:59.370
Well, it's like all these people that, you know, we're talking about birds, you know, dying outside our window, and they look up, and a bird is dying outside their window.
嗯，就像那些人一样，你知道，我们谈论着窗外死去的鸟，他们抬头一看，窗外正好有一只鸟在死。

130
00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.470
What is that?
那到底是怎么回事？

131
00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:01.310
I don't know.
我不知道。

132
00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:01.950
Ooh.
噢。

133
00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:02.790
Ah.
啊。

134
00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:03.710
All right.
好吧。

135
00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:06.170
Well, listen, that's all we got.
好了，听着，我们今天就到这儿了。

136
00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:09.410
Please enjoy our breakdown of beach games.
请尽情享受我们对《海滩游戏》的解析。

137
00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:09.930
Great.
太棒了。

138
00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.170
And hopefully you won't get anything in your eye.
希望你们的眼睛都不会进东西。

139
00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:13.550
Wear some sunglasses.
戴上墨镜吧。

140
00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.110
Yeah, while you listen.
没错，听的时候戴上。

141
00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:16.450
Good idea, lady.
好主意，女士。

142
00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:16.810
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

143
00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:21.840
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

144
00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.160
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

145
00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.420
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

146
00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:25.660
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

147
00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:29.500
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office Rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档《办公室》终极重温播客。

148
00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:36.480
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

149
00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:37.660
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

150
00:07:41.450 --> 00:07:41.890
Angela.
安吉拉。

151
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:42.710
Hey!
嘿！

152
00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.350
We are so excited today, you guys.
大家伙儿，我们今天太兴奋了。

153
00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.390
We're going to the beach today.
我们今天要出发去海滩了。

154
00:07:48.710 --> 00:07:50.790
We're going to play some beach games.
我们要去玩一些海滩游戏。

155
00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:52.290
Yes!
耶！

156
00:07:52.870 --> 00:07:59.090
Season 3, episode 22, written by Jen Salata and Greg Daniels, directed by Harold Ramis.
第三季第22集，编剧是Jen Salata和Greg Daniels，导演是Harold Ramis。

157
00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.410
It's beach games.
这一集是《海滩游戏》。

158
00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.290
We have so much to talk about.
我们要聊的内容实在太多了。

159
00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:04.970
I kind of feel like we just got to get to it.
我觉得我们得赶紧开始了。

160
00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:07.810
We should dive in because I took very diligent notes.
我们应该直接切入正题，因为我做了非常详尽的笔记。

161
00:08:08.410 --> 00:08:10.310
And I think you did in real life.
而且我觉得你在现实生活中也做了笔记。

162
00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:11.670
We'll get to that.
我们待会儿会聊到那个。

163
00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.090
All right.
好的。

164
00:08:13.190 --> 00:08:13.990
Here's a summary.
这是剧情梗概。

165
00:08:14.850 --> 00:08:18.690
Michael is invited to interview for a job opening at corporate.
迈克尔受邀去公司总部面试一个空缺职位。

166
00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:27.890
Certain that he's a lock for the job, he takes his employees to the beach at Lake Scranton and holds a series of challenges to determine his successor.
他确信自己稳拿这份工作，于是带着员工们去了斯克兰顿湖，并举行了一系列挑战来选定他的继任者。

167
00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:32.450
At the end of the day, Michael sets up a cold walk as a final challenge.
在一天结束时，迈克尔设置了一场“煤炭行走”作为终极挑战。

168
00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:39.710
Pam does the cold walk and summons up the courage to tell Jim and the whole office her real feelings.
帕姆完成了煤炭行走，并鼓起勇气向吉姆和整个办公室表达了她的真实感受。

169
00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:41.150
Oh, man.
天哪。

170
00:08:41.710 --> 00:08:45.110
That was so tough to watch.
那一幕看得我太难受了。

171
00:08:45.310 --> 00:08:46.910
It was beautiful, Jenna.
那很美，珍娜。

172
00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.870
Pam broke my heart in this episode.
这一集里的帕姆让我心碎。

173
00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:50.870
Yeah.
是啊。

174
00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:53.130
I had not seen this episode since it aired.
自从这一集播出后，我就没再看过。

175
00:08:54.990 --> 00:08:57.510
And it shocked me.
它让我感到震惊。

176
00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.370
And I did it.
虽然那是我演的。

177
00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.510
And I was still shocked.
但我依然感到震惊。

178
00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:02.830
Isn't that funny?
这难道不有趣吗？

179
00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:05.630
Like the way the brain works where you're like, wait, I did all that.
大脑的工作方式就是这样，你会想：等等，这些都是我做的吗？

180
00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.550
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

181
00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:07.610
That's kind of cool.
这感觉还挺酷的。

182
00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:08.590
Yeah.
是啊。

183
00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:15.130
So, fast fact number one, Angela, our beach games is set on Lake Scranton.
那么，第一个速览事实，安吉拉，我们的《海滩游戏》是在斯克兰顿湖拍摄的。

184
00:09:15.570 --> 00:09:16.010
Yes.
没错。

185
00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:21.050
Obviously, we didn't go to the real Lake Scranton, but I did want to just talk a little bit about it.
显然，我们并没有去真正的斯克兰顿湖，但我确实想简单聊聊它。

186
00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.270
Oh, let's hear it.
哦，说来听听。

187
00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:30.070
Well, Lake Scranton is actually a reservoir, and it was built with a dam in the early 1900s.
嗯，斯克兰顿湖实际上是一个水库，它是20世纪初通过修建大坝形成的。

188
00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:42.030
The dam was built by William Walker Scranton, and the body of water it created was originally called the Burnt Bridge Reservoir, although the public calls it Lake Scranton.
大坝是由威廉·沃克·斯克兰顿修建的，它形成的水域最初被称为“烧桥水库”，尽管公众称它为斯克兰顿湖。

189
00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:49.630
Well, Jenna, you and I have both been to Scranton, and one of the times that I went, they drove me around Lake Scranton, and it is so pretty.
嗯，珍娜，你我都去过斯克兰顿，有一次我去的时候，他们开车带我绕了斯克兰顿湖一圈，那里真的很美。

190
00:09:51.290 --> 00:10:00.830
There is a running track around the real Lake Scranton, and it's absolutely gorgeous, but I did look up a few facts about it, Ange.
真正的斯克兰顿湖周围有一条跑道，景色绝对迷人，不过安吉，我确实查了一些关于它的事实。

191
00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:01.310
Yeah?
是吗？

192
00:10:02.410 --> 00:10:04.090
Swimming is not permitted.
那里禁止游泳。

193
00:10:05.470 --> 00:10:09.090
Boating is not permitted, but canoeing and kayaking is allowed.
禁止划船，但允许划独木舟和皮划艇。

194
00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.770
I wonder why you can't swim in it.
我纳闷为什么不能在里面游泳。

195
00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.090
Like, I get the no motor, right?
比如，我理解禁止机动船，对吧？

196
00:10:13.310 --> 00:10:13.890
That's like...
那就像是……

197
00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:13.990
Right.
没错。

198
00:10:13.990 --> 00:10:18.070
Like, I think that's sort of really cool, but I wonder why they're no swimming.
我觉得那挺酷的，但我很好奇为什么禁止游泳。

199
00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:19.350
I don't know.
我不知道。

200
00:10:19.590 --> 00:10:19.810
Hmm.
嗯。

201
00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:21.130
I'm not sure.
我不确定。

202
00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:21.990
We're intrigued.
我们很感兴趣。

203
00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:23.230
Scranton, write us.
斯克兰顿，写信给我们吧。

204
00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:24.850
Tell us why you can't swim in your lake.
告诉我们为什么你们不能在湖里游泳。

205
00:10:26.150 --> 00:10:29.310
Well, this leads me to fast fact number two.
嗯，这引出了我的第二个速览事实。

206
00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:40.810
I brought up all these facts about Lake Scranton because we had a fan question from Sophia B., Aaron W., Dana D., Maren B., and Faye B.
我之所以提到所有关于斯克兰顿湖的事实，是因为我们收到了来自索菲亚·B、亚伦·W、达娜·D、马伦·B和费伊·B的粉丝提问。

207
00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:44.750
Where was the beach that you filmed this episode?
你们拍摄这一集的海滩在哪里？

208
00:10:45.650 --> 00:10:49.950
Was it a long commute, and how many days did you film at that location?
通勤时间长吗？你们在那个地点拍摄了几天？

209
00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.010
Well, I will tell you.
嗯，我会告诉你们的。

210
00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.330
Tell us.
告诉我们吧。

211
00:10:54.550 --> 00:10:55.410
I know.
我知道。

212
00:10:55.610 --> 00:10:59.750
I remember one or two things, but I bet you got all the details, so let's hear it.
我记得一两件事，但我敢说你掌握了所有细节，所以让我们听听吧。

213
00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:02.950
Well, I reached out to Kentopedia, and here's what he told me.
嗯，我联系了肯托百科（Kentopedia），这是他告诉我的。

214
00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:08.250
We filmed at the beach at the Hanson Dam Recreation Center in Sylmar.
我们在希尔马的汉森大坝娱乐中心的海滩拍摄的。

215
00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:11.110
We shot there for four days and nights.
我们在那里拍摄了四个昼夜。

216
00:11:11.450 --> 00:11:14.250
Well, you mentioned that you've been to the real Lake Scranton.
嗯，你提到过你去过真正的斯克兰顿湖。

217
00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:20.390
I've been to this real Hanson Dam Recreation Center outside of us filming.
除了拍摄之外，我还去过这个真正的汉森大坝娱乐中心。

218
00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:21.230
You have?
你去过？

219
00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:28.290
Yes, because there is this museum, this children's museum called the Discovery Cube that's right nearby.
是的，因为附近有一个博物馆，一个叫“探索立方体”的儿童博物馆。

220
00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:34.270
And when you go through this area, there's also like an equestrian center.
当你经过这个区域时，还有一个马术中心。

221
00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:35.550
There's an aquatic center.
有一个水上中心。

222
00:11:35.810 --> 00:11:37.170
There's a playground.
还有一个游乐场。

223
00:11:37.650 --> 00:11:47.150
Because, lady, the place that they put us to film this episode was like you had – I had no idea all this stuff was there.
因为，女士，他们安排我们拍摄这一集的地方，我根本不知道那里有这么多设施。

224
00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:56.750
My memory of where we filmed was it was like a chemical pond runoff, like from a dam, where I was like, are we like breathing in fumes?
我对拍摄地点的记忆是，它就像大坝流出的化学池塘水，当时我在想，我们是不是在吸入废气？

225
00:11:56.930 --> 00:11:59.730
It was really like gross.
感觉真的很恶心。

226
00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:10.130
They – maybe like the only place they let you film is in this like weird janky corner of this area.
他们——也许他们唯一允许拍摄的地方就是这个区域里一个奇怪又破烂的角落。

227
00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.350
Where the runoff water goes.
就是废水流向的地方。

228
00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:16.550
Yeah, because this recreation center is actually really nice.
是啊，因为这个娱乐中心其实非常不错。

229
00:12:16.850 --> 00:12:19.690
But here's something I found out too.
但我也发现了这一点。

230
00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:23.790
The lake where we filmed is filled with circulated drinking water.
我们拍摄的那个湖里装的是循环饮用水。

231
00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:24.470
What?
什么？

232
00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:29.250
Yeah, circulated drinking water, and it offers fishing and public boating.
是的，循环饮用水，而且那里还提供钓鱼和公共划船项目。

233
00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.510
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

234
00:12:32.490 --> 00:12:37.310
So when Ed is out there floating in the water, he was in some recycled drinking water.
所以当艾德在水里漂浮时，他是在循环饮用水里。

235
00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:38.770
Oh, well, that's good to know.
哦，那真是好消息。

236
00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:42.910
All these years, I worried for him that he was going to get like some kind of weird rash.
这么多年来，我一直担心他会得什么奇怪的皮疹。

237
00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:47.710
All right.
好的。

238
00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:50.150
Well, let's move on to fastback number three.
那么，让我们进入第三个速览事实。

239
00:12:51.030 --> 00:13:01.270
So like we said earlier, this was written by both Greg Daniels and Jen Salata, and we reached out to Jen Salata, and she sent us audio clips.
正如我们之前所说，这一集是由格雷格·丹尼尔斯和简·萨拉塔共同编写的，我们联系了简·萨拉塔，她给我们发来了音频片段。

240
00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:02.890
She sent us so many.
她发了好多。

241
00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:04.210
She's so gracious.
她真是太客气了。

242
00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:08.430
We're going to sprinkle them throughout, but here she has one for us right now.
我们会把它们穿插在节目中，现在她就有一段要给我们听。

243
00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:16.670
Yes, she is going to tell us a little bit about the inspiration for this episode and what it was like to write a script with Greg.
是的，她要给我们讲讲这一集的灵感来源，以及和格雷格一起写剧本是什么感觉。

244
00:13:16.950 --> 00:13:21.210
I think the inspiration for this episode was just Survivor.
我想这一集的灵感来源就是《幸存者》节目。

245
00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:22.930
I think it was Greg's idea.
我想这是格雷格的主意。

246
00:13:22.930 --> 00:13:30.650
And I remember all of us talking about Survivor being a perfect way for Michael Scott to pick his successor.
我记得我们大家都在讨论《幸存者》是迈克尔·斯科特挑选继任者的完美方式。

247
00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:37.730
I mean, what other way would this man use to try to pick somebody who could run a branch?
我是说，除了这种方式，这个男人还会用什么方法来挑选能管理分公司的人呢？

248
00:13:37.730 --> 00:13:42.410
It just seemed like a no-brainer for Michael Scott to do it this way.
对迈克尔·斯科特来说，用这种方式简直是不假思索的选择。

249
00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:47.110
And then we tried to sit down and write the whole thing together, and we were like, this isn't going to work.
然后我们试着坐下来一起写完整部剧本，但我们发现这行不通。

250
00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.410
So we divided it up.
所以我们把它分开了。

251
00:13:48.810 --> 00:13:52.150
We can't remember exactly how we did it.
我们记不清具体是怎么写的了。

252
00:13:52.150 --> 00:13:57.290
I think sometimes with Paul, when I'd write a script with Paul, I'd do the first half, he'd do the second, or vice versa.
我觉得有时候和保罗合作，写剧本时我会写前半部分，他写后半部分，或者反过来。

253
00:13:57.510 --> 00:14:01.910
And with Greg, I think we didn't do cleanly divided up that way.
至于格雷格，我觉得我们没有那样明确地分工。

254
00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.490
I think just he did some of the scenes, I did others.
我想就是他写了一些场景，我写了另一些。

255
00:14:04.670 --> 00:14:13.390
And I do remember that the Pam speech was mostly Greg, and I think that is such a beautiful part of the episode.
我确实记得帕姆的那段演讲主要是格雷格写的，我觉得那是这一集中非常精彩的部分。

256
00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:19.010
And the Pam arc preexisted the idea of the Beach Games episode.
而且帕姆的故事线在“海滩游戏”这一集构思出来之前就已经存在了。

257
00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:23.350
So I think some of the ideas from that speech were in his notes.
所以我认为那段演讲中的一些想法就在他的笔记里。

258
00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:25.710
But I love that part.
但我很喜欢那部分。

259
00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:28.890
It is one of my favorite parts, if not my favorite part of the episode.
那是我最喜欢的片段之一，甚至可以说是这一集中我最喜欢的部分。

260
00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:31.670
So credit to Greg for that part, for sure.
所以那部分绝对要归功于格雷格。

261
00:14:31.830 --> 00:14:33.450
But we both wrote a bunch of it.
不过我们俩确实都写了很多内容。

262
00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:35.710
I just don't think we clearly divided it up.
我只是觉得我们没有明确地划分过。

263
00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:44.170
Well, Ange, I remember Greg talking to me about this Pam arc of her finding her voice.
嗯，安吉，我记得格雷格跟我谈过帕姆寻找自我声音的这条故事线。

264
00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:44.510
Yeah.
是的。

265
00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:49.990
And he planted this idea a few episodes ago, and we sprinkled it in.
他在几集之前就埋下了这个伏笔，我们把它穿插在剧情里。

266
00:14:50.490 --> 00:14:58.130
And so I just love this idea that he'd been maybe writing down little notes about what Pam will finally say when she says something.
所以我很喜欢这个想法，也许他一直在记下一些小笔记，关于帕姆最终会说出什么样的话。

267
00:14:58.130 --> 00:15:05.610
And I remember getting the script for this episode and just being so excited as an actor.
我记得拿到这一集的剧本时，作为演员我感到非常兴奋。

268
00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.590
There was just so much to chew on.
有太多值得细细品味的东西了。

269
00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:12.390
I mean, I thought that it was just beautifully done.
我是说，我觉得这写得太棒了。

270
00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:20.070
Really, just Pam's whole journey this season about even her sending the wrong beer back.
真的，帕姆这一整季的旅程，甚至包括她退掉那杯错误的啤酒。

271
00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:20.990
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

272
00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:28.450
And just having these moments where she stood up for herself and spoke her truth, and it all builds to this one moment.
还有那些她坚持自我、说出真心话的时刻，这一切都汇聚到了这一刻。

273
00:15:28.470 --> 00:15:30.870
And it's just so well done.
真的做得太好了。

274
00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:37.650
When I was re-watching this, I was marveling at what a well-written episode this was.
重看这一集时，我惊叹于这集剧本写得有多出色。

275
00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:38.670
Yes.
没错。

276
00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:44.350
Well, maybe we should take a quick break and then come back and break down this episode.
好吧，也许我们该休息一下，回来后再深入剖析这一集。

277
00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:45.150
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

278
00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:46.910
Jenna, we have so much to talk about.
珍娜，我们要聊的实在太多了。

279
00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:47.930
I know.
我知道。

280
00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.130
We've been trading a lot of texts about this one.
关于这一集我们已经互发了很多短信讨论了。

281
00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:59.840
All right.
好的。

282
00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:02.720
So this episode starts with this very funny cold open.
这一集是以一个非常有趣的冷开场开始的。

283
00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:05.020
It is Dwight and Michael.
是德怀特和迈克尔。

284
00:16:05.260 --> 00:16:06.420
They're in Michael's office.
他们在迈克尔的办公室里。

285
00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:09.060
And Michael's convinced that he's sick, you guys.
迈克尔坚信自己病了，伙计们。

286
00:16:09.060 --> 00:16:09.920
He's convinced.
他非常确信。

287
00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:12.440
They're scrolling through a website.
他们在浏览一个网站。

288
00:16:12.440 --> 00:16:16.940
It's like WebMD or something, trying to figure out what he is sick from.
就像WebMD之类的，试图找出他得了什么病。

289
00:16:17.060 --> 00:16:18.200
Dwight's very concerned.
德怀特非常担心。

290
00:16:19.100 --> 00:16:19.380
Yes.
是的。

291
00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:23.480
Pam has a talking head where she explains that this happens about 40 times a year.
帕姆有个访谈镜头，解释说这种情况一年大约会发生40次。

292
00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.960
Michael, it's sick that has no symptoMs.
迈克尔，这是一种没有症状的病。

293
00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:27.940
Yes.
没错。

294
00:16:27.940 --> 00:16:32.500
Well, Jen left us a really great audio clip about this, about the inspiration for this
嗯，简给我们留下了一段很棒的音频片段，关于这个冷开场的灵感来源。

295
00:16:32.500 --> 00:16:33.100
cold open.
冷开场。

296
00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:34.420
Sam, can you play that?
萨姆，能播放一下吗？

297
00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:37.900
Greg and I wrote the episode together and it was really fun.
格雷格和我一起写了这一集，真的很有趣。

298
00:16:38.220 --> 00:16:42.580
I remember being really curious, what is Greg's process going to be like?
我记得当时很好奇，格雷格的创作过程会是什么样的？

299
00:16:42.740 --> 00:16:46.280
Because writing scripts, it was such a solitary part of what we did.
因为写剧本是我们工作中非常孤独的一部分。

300
00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:50.480
And so I was always wondering, like, what are other writers like when they go off to write
所以我总是很好奇，其他编剧在去写剧本时是什么样的。

301
00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:50.840
a script?
剧本吗？

302
00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:56.880
It became quickly obvious that his process at the beginning was like mine, which is like
很快我就发现，他刚开始的创作过程跟我一样，

303
00:16:56.880 --> 00:17:01.240
every other writer I've ever met, which is there's a fair amount of procrastinating right
跟我见过的所有其他作家一样，那就是在真正开始艰苦工作之前，

304
00:17:01.240 --> 00:17:03.000
away before you have to get into the hard work.
会先花相当长的时间拖延。

305
00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.720
It's figuring out what you want to eat.
比如琢磨想吃什么。

306
00:17:04.900 --> 00:17:06.000
It's sharpening your pencils.
比如削铅笔。

307
00:17:06.020 --> 00:17:08.240
It's figuring out the temperature of the room.
比如调整房间的温度。

308
00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:16.580
And for both of us, we started focusing on ailments, like what was wrong, how we weren't
我们俩当时都开始关注各种小毛病，比如哪里不舒服，身体状况如何，

309
00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:17.540
feeling well.
感觉不太好。

310
00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:20.940
Like my ear was bothering him and he wasn't feeling super well at the time.
比如我的耳朵当时让他很困扰，而他自己当时也感觉不太舒服。

311
00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:24.940
And so we went on WebMD and we tried to diagnose ourselves and each other.
于是我们上了WebMD网站，试图给自己和对方诊断。

312
00:17:26.240 --> 00:17:31.740
And they used to have a little body where you could like point to the part of the body that
网站上以前有个小人模型，你可以点选身体上

