899
00:44:31.650 --> 00:44:32.710
Are you like a basketball fan?
你是篮球迷吗？

900
00:44:32.710 --> 00:44:34.410
And where's all this lingo coming from?
这些术语都是从哪冒出来的？

901
00:44:35.170 --> 00:44:36.250
I play basketball.
我打篮球。

902
00:44:36.410 --> 00:44:37.050
I play JV.
我打校二队。

903
00:44:37.230 --> 00:44:40.950
And then when everyone got really tall, I had to stop playing because I was too short.
后来大家都长得很高了，我因为太矮不得不放弃了。

904
00:44:40.970 --> 00:44:42.590
And we had a really good point guard.
我们当时有个很棒的控球后卫。

905
00:44:42.790 --> 00:44:44.870
So then I became a basketball cheerleader.
所以我后来成了篮球啦啦队员。

906
00:44:45.070 --> 00:44:47.610
And I was also the manager on the basketball team.
我还当过篮球队的经理。

907
00:44:48.090 --> 00:44:51.290
And I was also a mascot one basketball season.
有一个篮球赛季我还当过吉祥物。

908
00:44:51.290 --> 00:44:52.730
And I love basketball.
我真的很爱篮球。

909
00:44:52.950 --> 00:44:54.950
And we have a hoop in our driveway.
我们车道上就有个篮筐。

910
00:44:54.950 --> 00:44:56.410
And we play all the time.
我们经常在那儿打球。

911
00:44:56.450 --> 00:44:58.250
And I have a fantastic outside shot.
我的外线投篮特别准。

912
00:44:58.390 --> 00:44:59.910
And I often win at horse.
玩“马”游戏时我经常赢。

913
00:45:02.480 --> 00:45:07.580
Angela, I'm clapping because people couldn't see me bowing down to you.
安吉拉，我鼓掌是因为大家看不见我在向你鞠躬致敬。

914
00:45:09.060 --> 00:45:11.620
But I mean, I'm speechless.
我是说，我简直无言以对。

915
00:45:12.260 --> 00:45:14.140
I did not know this about you.
关于你的这些事我竟然一点都不知道。

916
00:45:14.340 --> 00:45:18.080
And also, I mean, I defer to you here.
而且，我是说，在这方面我甘拜下风。

917
00:45:18.220 --> 00:45:22.240
If this were a debate and someone had to win, you won.
如果这是一场辩论，非要分出胜负的话，你赢了。

918
00:45:22.460 --> 00:45:23.540
I mean, that was juSt...
我是说，那简直……

919
00:45:24.240 --> 00:45:28.180
I want you to know, it's not out yet, but I have this Advil commercial where I have to
我想让你知道，虽然还没播出，但我拍过一个艾德维尔止痛药的广告，里面我得

920
00:45:28.180 --> 00:45:28.820
shoot baskets.
投篮。

921
00:45:28.820 --> 00:45:31.140
And I made like 13 baskets in a row.
我当时连进了大概13个球。

922
00:45:31.220 --> 00:45:33.560
And one of them they used in the actual shot.
他们把其中一个镜头用在了正片里。

923
00:45:33.700 --> 00:45:37.720
And I was so happy that they showed the whole shot because I was like, I made that sucker.
我当时特别高兴他们把整个投篮过程都剪进去了，因为我心想，那球可是我投进的。

924
00:45:38.940 --> 00:45:42.860
You were Brian Baumgartner while shooting the basketball episode.
你在拍篮球那集的时候简直就是布莱恩·鲍姆加特纳附体。

925
00:45:43.000 --> 00:45:47.280
You have like a secret basketball skill that no one knew about.
你竟然有种没人知道的篮球绝活。

926
00:45:47.280 --> 00:45:51.100
Don't you remember the basketball hoop by our trailers and we would play horse?
你不记得我们拖车旁边的那个篮筐了吗？我们以前常在那儿玩“马”游戏。

927
00:45:51.100 --> 00:45:53.500
I was always out there with the guys playing horse.
我总是和男同事们在那儿玩“马”游戏。

928
00:45:53.760 --> 00:45:54.920
I do remember that.
我确实记得。

929
00:45:55.000 --> 00:45:56.040
And I have a picture of it.
我还有张照片呢。

930
00:45:56.140 --> 00:45:56.280
Yeah.
是啊。

931
00:45:57.340 --> 00:46:00.200
Well, listen, I feel like we've gone off topic.
好吧，听着，我觉得我们跑题了。

932
00:46:00.740 --> 00:46:01.180
You think?
你觉得呢？

933
00:46:01.600 --> 00:46:03.620
Wait, we're back to the hot dogs, guys.
等等，我们要回到热狗的话题上了，各位。

934
00:46:03.820 --> 00:46:04.700
Back to the hot dogs.
回到热狗的话题。

935
00:46:05.280 --> 00:46:06.860
Andy wins the competition.
安迪赢了比赛。

936
00:46:07.280 --> 00:46:10.640
But this was an arduous scene for everyone to shoot.
但这对于所有人来说都是一场艰苦的戏。

937
00:46:10.860 --> 00:46:14.520
I was really lucky, Jenna, because I said my character's a vegetarian.
我真的很幸运，珍娜，因为我说过我的角色是素食主义者。

938
00:46:14.780 --> 00:46:16.280
She's not going to be eating these.
她不会吃这些东西的。

939
00:46:16.280 --> 00:46:18.160
I made a really big plea about that.
我为此极力争取过。

940
00:46:19.640 --> 00:46:27.040
But poor Brian and Ed, Leslie, all those guys were shoving hot dogs in their face.
但可怜的布莱恩、艾德、莱斯利，还有其他人，都得往嘴里塞热狗。

941
00:46:27.200 --> 00:46:30.220
And Jenna, do you remember they were starting to gag?
珍娜，你还记得他们当时都开始干呕了吗？

942
00:46:30.720 --> 00:46:31.700
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

943
00:46:32.240 --> 00:46:32.440
Yeah.
记得。

944
00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:36.120
You know, we got a fan question from Caitlin Mulvihill who said,
你知道吗，我们收到一个粉丝凯特琳·马尔维希尔的问题，她问，

945
00:46:36.260 --> 00:46:40.440
how many times did you have to film the hot dog contest scene?
你们拍热狗大赛那场戏拍了多少次？

946
00:46:40.600 --> 00:46:43.340
And did you have to eat all the hot dogs every time?
而且你们每次都得把热狗全吃掉吗？

947
00:46:44.260 --> 00:46:47.740
I just remember it took a long time.
我只记得拍了很久。

948
00:46:48.100 --> 00:46:51.860
It was a lot of angles, a lot of coverage.
有很多机位，拍了很多素材。

949
00:46:52.160 --> 00:46:53.620
A lot of reaction shots.
还有很多反应镜头。

950
00:46:53.780 --> 00:46:55.300
We were there for like half a day.
我们在那儿待了大概半天。

951
00:46:56.220 --> 00:46:56.500
Yeah.
没错。

952
00:46:56.820 --> 00:47:03.340
And Jen, we asked Jen, what was the hardest stunt during beach games?
还有珍，我们问了珍，海滩运动会里最难的特技是什么？

953
00:47:04.300 --> 00:47:06.180
And this is what she had to say.
这是她的回答。

954
00:47:06.180 --> 00:47:11.740
I think the answer for what was the hardest stunt of this episode depends on who you ask.
我觉得关于这集最难特技的答案，取决于你问的是谁。

955
00:47:11.900 --> 00:47:16.780
I think for the actors, it was possibly the hot dog eating conteSt.
对演员来说，我觉得可能是热狗大赛。

956
00:47:16.780 --> 00:47:18.340
I'm curious what you guys think.
我很好奇你们怎么看。

957
00:47:18.480 --> 00:47:20.280
I remember spit buckets.
我记得有吐食桶。

958
00:47:20.280 --> 00:47:24.440
I could be wrong about that, but I'm fairly certain there were a bunch of spit buckets.
我可能记错了，但我相当确定当时有很多吐食桶。

959
00:47:24.640 --> 00:47:27.580
But there was some actual eating of hot dogs.
但他们确实吃了不少热狗。

960
00:47:27.640 --> 00:47:32.280
And I think Ed Helms ate an enormous amount of hot dogs, if I remember correctly.
如果我没记错的话，艾德·赫尔姆斯吃掉了巨量的热狗。

961
00:47:32.280 --> 00:47:36.880
I think he was going really hard for winning the conteSt.
我觉得他为了赢下比赛真的很拼。

962
00:47:37.260 --> 00:47:41.720
So I think that that was probably a lot of people's answers.
所以我认为那可能是很多人的答案。

963
00:47:41.880 --> 00:47:49.520
For me, it was getting the shot during the Michael talking head of Andy floating away at sea.
对我来说，最难的是拍迈克尔关于安迪漂流到海上的那段采访镜头。

964
00:47:50.160 --> 00:47:51.900
Yes, we will get to that.
没错，我们待会儿会讲到那个。

965
00:47:52.120 --> 00:47:55.700
She sent in some more amazing stuff about that stunt.
她发来了一些关于那个特技的精彩内容。

966
00:47:55.700 --> 00:47:59.300
But I do remember the spit buckets, Ange.
但我确实记得吐食桶的事，安吉。

967
00:47:59.480 --> 00:48:00.240
I do too.
我也记得。

968
00:48:00.240 --> 00:48:06.780
And one of the things, you guys, on some shows, the way they shoot, you know when you're on camera.
而且有一点，各位，在有些节目里，拍摄方式是让你知道什么时候在镜头里。

969
00:48:06.940 --> 00:48:10.680
And when you're off camera, you don't have to sort of participate.
当你不在镜头里时，你就不必参与其中。

970
00:48:10.680 --> 00:48:13.380
You can kind of not eat, right?
你可以不用吃，对吧？

971
00:48:13.680 --> 00:48:17.420
But the way we shot this, there was a huge group shot, right?
但我们这次的拍摄方式是全景大镜头，对吧？

972
00:48:17.500 --> 00:48:19.440
There's a camera that's capturing everything.
有一台摄像机在捕捉一切。

973
00:48:19.440 --> 00:48:25.900
So these guys had to eat on every take because they never knew when the camera was specifically on them or not.
所以这些人每一条都得吃，因为他们不知道摄像机什么时候正好对着他们。

974
00:48:25.900 --> 00:48:33.560
And I remember when they would yell, cut, immediately, like the prop guys would run over with buckets.
我记得每次导演喊“卡”的时候，道具组的人就会立刻跑过来拿着桶。

975
00:48:33.560 --> 00:48:37.560
And these guys would all start spitting in the buckets because they couldn't have the buckets on the ground.
这些人就开始往桶里吐，因为桶不能放在地上。

976
00:48:37.660 --> 00:48:39.360
There was nowhere to hide them, right?
没地方藏，对吧？

977
00:48:40.140 --> 00:48:42.840
And so the prop guys would run over with the buckets.
所以道具组的人会跑过来拿着桶。

978
00:48:42.980 --> 00:48:45.500
And Ed said this thing in the DVD commentary.
艾德在DVD评论音轨里说过这件事。

979
00:48:45.600 --> 00:48:51.540
He said, first of all, spitting out food that I've been chewing and holding in my mouth,
他说，首先，把嚼过并含在嘴里的食物吐出来，

980
00:48:52.380 --> 00:48:57.460
the action of spitting out this chewed food would activate my gag reflex.
这种吐出咀嚼过的食物的动作会触发我的呕吐反射。

981
00:48:57.460 --> 00:48:59.280
So I'd start gagging.
所以我就会开始干呕。

982
00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:03.540
And he said, but then on top of that, this bucket that they would bring around,
他说，更糟糕的是，他们拿过来的那个桶里，

983
00:49:03.780 --> 00:49:06.820
several other people had spit their food out into.
已经有其他好几个人吐过食物了。

984
00:49:07.040 --> 00:49:08.320
He said, just all of it.
他说，简直是……全都是。

985
00:49:08.520 --> 00:49:09.280
All of it.
全都是。

986
00:49:09.320 --> 00:49:12.680
He said, like, they were all getting so grossed out.
他说，他们当时都觉得恶心透了。

987
00:49:13.820 --> 00:49:20.100
Well, this scene really reminded me of that birthday cake scene from Meredith's birthday.
这场景真的让我想起了梅瑞狄斯生日那天吃生日蛋糕的场景。

988
00:49:21.060 --> 00:49:23.220
Where we all ate cake.
我们当时都在吃蛋糕。

989
00:49:23.640 --> 00:49:25.100
Mint chocolate chip ice cream cake.
薄荷巧克力碎冰淇淋蛋糕。

990
00:49:25.280 --> 00:49:26.440
I can't eat it to this day.
直到今天我都吃不了那个。

991
00:49:26.440 --> 00:49:27.660
I can't eat it.
我吃不了。

992
00:49:28.380 --> 00:49:28.640
Same.
我也是。

993
00:49:29.180 --> 00:49:34.060
We ate so much of it because we never knew when we were on camera.
我们吃了那么多，因为我们永远不知道什么时候在镜头里。

994
00:49:34.280 --> 00:49:44.080
And then like that, I feel like there's barely any footage in this episode of these guys eating the hot dogs.
而且就像那样，我觉得这一集里几乎没什么他们吃热狗的镜头。

995
00:49:44.240 --> 00:49:48.340
It does not accurately reflect how much hot dog eating happened.
这根本无法准确反映他们到底吃了多少热狗。

996
00:49:48.660 --> 00:49:49.540
Not at all.
完全没有。

997
00:49:49.740 --> 00:49:50.620
These poor guys.
这些可怜的家伙。

998
00:49:51.800 --> 00:49:54.420
And Jim isn't eating the hot dogs.
而且吉姆没吃热狗。

999
00:49:54.420 --> 00:49:59.040
There's a deleted scene where he brought a tuna salad and he is not even participating.
有个删减片段是他带了金枪鱼沙拉，他甚至都没参与。

1000
00:49:59.360 --> 00:50:01.460
So John did not have to do this.
所以约翰根本不用受这份罪。

1001
00:50:01.660 --> 00:50:02.740
And neither did I.
我也没有。

1002
00:50:02.940 --> 00:50:04.060
And neither did Steve.
史蒂夫也没有。

1003
00:50:04.920 --> 00:50:05.960
Oh, God.
天哪。

1004
00:50:06.420 --> 00:50:07.160
Well, Jenna.
好吧，珍娜。

1005
00:50:07.600 --> 00:50:10.760
So Andy wins with 13 hot dogs.
所以安迪以13个热狗赢了。

1006
00:50:11.140 --> 00:50:11.260
Right?
对吧？

1007
00:50:11.560 --> 00:50:12.040
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1008
00:50:12.320 --> 00:50:12.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1009
00:50:12.940 --> 00:50:19.080
I just looked up this year the hot dog eating contest, the Nathan's hot dog eating contest for 2020.
我刚查了今年的热狗大赛，就是2020年的内森热狗大赛。

1010
00:50:19.780 --> 00:50:20.780
Did you too?
你也查了吗？

1011
00:50:20.980 --> 00:50:21.580
Did you too?
你也查了吗？

1012
00:50:22.420 --> 00:50:25.060
Because I've been to the hot dog eating conteSt.
因为我曾经去过热狗大赛现场。

1013
00:50:25.480 --> 00:50:25.920
What?
什么？

1014
00:50:26.540 --> 00:50:27.120
Yeah.
是啊。

1015
00:50:27.480 --> 00:50:27.940
When?
什么时候？

1016
00:50:29.080 --> 00:50:30.240
In 2011.
2011年。

1017
00:50:31.240 --> 00:50:31.820
What?
什么？

1018
00:50:32.000 --> 00:50:32.260
How?
怎么会？

1019
00:50:32.260 --> 00:50:32.400
Why?
为什么？

1020
00:50:32.400 --> 00:50:33.680
I went to Coney Island.
我去了康尼岛。

1021
00:50:33.960 --> 00:50:35.880
Lee and I were in New York.
我和李当时在纽约。

1022
00:50:36.220 --> 00:50:40.240
We were looking for something to do over July 4th weekend.
我们想在7月4日那个周末找点事情做。

1023
00:50:40.600 --> 00:50:42.220
And you went to it?
然后你就去了？

1024
00:50:42.740 --> 00:50:48.420
We saw that the Coney Island hot dog eating, we got on the subway and we rode it out there.
我们看到有康尼岛热狗大赛，就坐地铁去了那里。

1025
00:50:48.940 --> 00:50:51.660
I was very pregnant.
当时我怀着孕。

1026
00:50:52.020 --> 00:50:54.700
I was like seven months pregnant.
大概怀孕七个月了。

1027
00:50:55.280 --> 00:50:56.500
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1028
00:50:57.120 --> 00:50:58.940
I did not know any of this.
这些我一点都不知道。

1029
00:50:59.080 --> 00:51:00.860
See, you think you know your best friend.
你看，你以为你很了解你最好的朋友。

1030
00:51:01.060 --> 00:51:05.540
And then all of a sudden she's going to hot dog eating contest and she knows how to play basketball.
结果突然发现她去过热狗大赛，而且还会打篮球。

1031
00:51:06.320 --> 00:51:07.600
Yeah, exactly.
没错，就是这样。

1032
00:51:07.600 --> 00:51:09.860
And here's my memory.
这是我的记忆。

1033
00:51:09.860 --> 00:51:11.480
It was super exciting.
当时超级兴奋。

1034
00:51:11.660 --> 00:51:13.140
We only saw the men's conteSt.
我们只看了男子组的比赛。

1035
00:51:13.140 --> 00:51:16.860
I saw Joey Chestnut win the hot dog eating conteSt.
我亲眼看到乔伊·切斯纳特赢得了热狗大赛。

1036
00:51:16.880 --> 00:51:18.680
He won again this year.
他今年又赢了。

1037
00:51:19.280 --> 00:51:22.660
Yeah, and he broke his world record this year.
是啊，而且他今年还打破了自己的世界纪录。

1038
00:51:22.800 --> 00:51:25.860
His nickname is Jaws, Joey Jaws Chestnut.
他的绰号是“大白鲨”，乔伊·“大白鲨”·切斯纳特。

1039
00:51:26.680 --> 00:51:34.700
Yeah, this year, because we both looked it up, Joey Chestnut ate 75 hot dogs and buns in 10 minutes.
没错，今年，因为我们俩都查了，乔伊·切斯纳特在10分钟内吃了75个热狗和面包。

1040
00:51:34.700 --> 00:51:42.520
And Jenna, in the female category, Miki Sudo ate 48 and a half hot dogs in 10 minutes and now has the new world record.
珍娜，在女子组，须藤美贵在10分钟内吃了48个半热狗，现在是新的世界纪录保持者。

1041
00:51:43.200 --> 00:51:49.120
Yeah, Joey Chestnut has won every year since 2007, with the exception of one year.
是的，乔伊·切斯纳特除了有一年没赢，从2007年开始每年都赢。

1042
00:51:49.420 --> 00:51:52.760
In 2015, Matt Stoney won.
2015年是马特·斯托尼赢的。

1043
00:51:53.440 --> 00:51:55.560
But Joey has won every year since.
但从那以后，乔伊每年都赢。

1044
00:51:56.300 --> 00:51:59.260
And Miki has won every year since 2014.
而须藤美贵从2014年开始每年都赢。

1045
00:51:59.780 --> 00:52:01.120
I will say one thing.
我得说一件事。

1046
00:52:01.120 --> 00:52:04.580
When I went to the hot dog eating contest, I mentioned I was very pregnant.
我去热狗大赛的时候，提到过我当时怀着孕。

1047
00:52:05.380 --> 00:52:07.780
I had to pee and there were no restrooMs.
我想上厕所，但那里没有洗手间。

1048
00:52:08.280 --> 00:52:17.500
And all of the businesses, because there's such a giant influx of people that come down, they all have signs that say no public restroom, no public restroom, no public restroom.
所有的商家，因为涌入的人潮实在太多了，都挂着牌子写着“不对外开放洗手间”，到处都是。

1049
00:52:17.620 --> 00:52:19.460
You can't just go in and use their bathroom.
你不能随便进去用他们的厕所。

1050
00:52:20.480 --> 00:52:27.540
But I found an employee at the Dunkin' Donuts who sneaked me in and let me use the bathroom there.
但我找到了一位唐恩都乐的员工，他偷偷带我进去，让我用了那里的洗手间。

1051
00:52:27.860 --> 00:52:28.140
Bless them.
祝福他们。

1052
00:52:28.520 --> 00:52:35.000
And I still, to this day, want to say thank you so much for helping me relieve my pregnant bladder that day.
直到今天，我依然想说非常感谢你那天帮我缓解了孕期的尿急。

1053
00:52:35.580 --> 00:52:38.200
Thank you, nice person at Dunkin' Donuts.
谢谢你，唐恩都乐那位好心人。

1054
00:52:38.460 --> 00:52:40.880
On Coney Island in 2011.
那是2011年在康尼岛。

1055
00:52:41.180 --> 00:52:47.720
You know, if you were Meredith, like the deleted scene, you would have just gone and squat in the bushes right by the bus.
你知道，如果你是梅雷迪思，就像那个删减片段里一样，你可能直接就在公交车旁边的灌木丛里蹲下了。

1056
00:52:48.220 --> 00:52:49.040
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1057
00:52:49.460 --> 00:52:50.260
Poor Kate.
可怜的凯特。

1058
00:52:50.460 --> 00:52:51.580
Kate in this episode.
这一集里的凯特。

1059
00:52:51.580 --> 00:52:52.320
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1060
00:52:52.880 --> 00:52:57.420
Well, maybe, Angela, on that note, we should take a break here and both use the restroom.
好吧，安吉拉，既然说到这儿了，我们或许该休息一下，都去趟洗手间。

1061
00:52:57.660 --> 00:52:57.940
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1062
00:52:58.460 --> 00:53:02.240
And then we'll come back with some sabotage.
然后回来聊聊蓄意破坏。

1063
00:53:03.360 --> 00:53:03.840
Sandwich.
三明治。

1064
00:53:04.100 --> 00:53:05.660
No, I said sandwich earlier.
不，我刚才说的是三明治。

1065
00:53:05.660 --> 00:53:07.520
This time I'm saying sabotage.
这次我说的是蓄意破坏。

1066
00:53:17.310 --> 00:53:19.290
Okay, we are back.
好了，我们回来了。

1067
00:53:19.710 --> 00:53:23.370
And, oh, Angela, I love this scene so much.
噢，安吉拉，我太喜欢这一幕了。

1068
00:53:23.510 --> 00:53:25.630
I rewound it and watched it twice.
我倒回去看了两遍。

1069
00:53:25.630 --> 00:53:25.830
Nice.
真棒。

1070
00:53:26.090 --> 00:53:27.370
I do love this scene.
我确实很喜欢这一幕。

1071
00:53:27.510 --> 00:53:28.350
It's one of my favorites.
这是我最喜欢的片段之一。

1072
00:53:29.310 --> 00:53:35.690
So this is the scene where Dwight and Angela have tiptoed away from the group.
这一幕是德怀特和安吉拉悄悄离开人群。

1073
00:53:35.910 --> 00:53:36.450
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1074
00:53:36.510 --> 00:53:40.090
And they're having a private conversation about sabotage.
他们正在私下讨论蓄意破坏的事。

1075
00:53:40.310 --> 00:53:43.130
Dwight would like Angela to sabotage her team.
德怀特想让安吉拉去破坏她所在的团队。

1076
00:53:43.470 --> 00:53:44.890
Yes, the ancient art.
没错，这门古老的艺术。

1077
00:53:45.510 --> 00:53:47.450
Like, Dutch sabotage.
比如，荷兰式破坏。

1078
00:53:47.510 --> 00:53:48.270
I was like, what?
我当时心想，什么？

1079
00:53:49.110 --> 00:53:50.890
This scene was so fun to film.
拍这一幕太有趣了。

1080
00:53:51.050 --> 00:53:56.350
First of all, I remember Jen and Harold and Rain and I trying to figure out where Dwight
首先，我记得珍、哈罗德、雷恩和我当时在琢磨德怀特和我

1081
00:53:56.350 --> 00:54:00.290
and I would be, where it would really look like we were away from everyone.
应该待在哪儿，才能看起来真的远离了所有人。

1082
00:54:00.710 --> 00:54:04.790
And also that we would think that we got away with it, right?
而且还要让我们觉得我们成功躲开了，对吧？

1083
00:54:05.170 --> 00:54:05.490
Yes.
是的。

1084
00:54:05.650 --> 00:54:08.290
And that the spy shot would have to be far enough away.
而且偷拍的镜头必须足够远。

1085
00:54:08.430 --> 00:54:09.330
So we did sort of climb.
所以我们确实爬了一段。

1086
00:54:09.470 --> 00:54:11.290
There were these little sand dunes, Jenna.
那里有一些小沙丘，珍娜。

1087
00:54:11.410 --> 00:54:11.790
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1088
00:54:12.010 --> 00:54:17.010
They were sort of small and they had like big sort of like tall kind of grass growing out of them.
它们有点小，上面长着那种高高的草。

1089
00:54:17.110 --> 00:54:19.430
Yeah, like reedy grass coming out of them.
对，就是那种长出来的芦苇草。

1090
00:54:19.830 --> 00:54:20.210
Itchy.
很扎人。

1091
00:54:20.330 --> 00:54:21.470
Itchy reedy grass.
扎人的芦苇草。

1092
00:54:21.650 --> 00:54:22.630
I remember it.
我记得。

1093
00:54:22.630 --> 00:54:24.750
It would kind of cut you a little if it touched your skin.
如果碰到皮肤，还会有点割人。

1094
00:54:25.130 --> 00:54:29.390
But we sort of tucked back in there for this scene.
但为了拍这一幕，我们还是躲进了那里。

1095
00:54:29.470 --> 00:54:31.370
And there are some great bloopers.
而且还有一些很棒的NG镜头。

1096
00:54:31.370 --> 00:54:35.610
And it's mostly just me laughing because I could not get through it.
大部分都是我在笑，因为我实在演不下去。

1097
00:54:35.630 --> 00:54:40.490
When he said sabotage and I said sandwich every single time.
他一说“蓄意破坏”，我每次都说成“三明治”。

1098
00:54:40.750 --> 00:54:42.550
The absurdity of these two.
这两个人真是荒唐透顶。

1099
00:54:43.050 --> 00:54:52.030
Not to mention, I could hear Jen Salata laughing from her little group of bushes where her and Harold were hiding.
更别提我还能听到珍·萨拉塔在她和哈罗德躲藏的那丛灌木后发出的笑声。

1100
00:54:52.710 --> 00:54:55.370
And I would be like, Jen, stop laughing.
我当时就想说，珍，别笑了。

1101
00:54:55.770 --> 00:54:57.310
I just got it together.
我刚把状态调整好。

1102
00:54:57.310 --> 00:54:58.710
And now Jen is laughing.
现在珍在笑。

1103
00:54:58.750 --> 00:55:00.110
And you couldn't see her.
而你没看见她。

1104
00:55:00.230 --> 00:55:02.190
It was just like this little clump of bushes that was like.
就像那一小丛灌木丛一样。

1105
00:55:04.150 --> 00:55:05.210
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

1106
00:55:05.250 --> 00:55:07.030
I love it so much.
我太喜欢了。

1107
00:55:07.690 --> 00:55:14.450
I love the end when Dwight says, if Michael organizes a group hug, stand next to me.
我特别喜欢结尾德怀特说的那句，如果迈克尔组织集体拥抱，就站在我旁边。

1108
00:55:14.690 --> 00:55:17.630
Jen told me she loved writing for Dwight and Angela.
珍告诉我她很喜欢为德怀特和安吉拉写戏。

1109
00:55:17.950 --> 00:55:21.730
That she loved their sort of suppressed love for one another.
因为她喜欢他们之间那种压抑的爱。

1110
00:55:22.630 --> 00:55:22.930
Yeah.
没错。

1111
00:55:23.530 --> 00:55:25.090
Oh, it's such a good scene.
噢，那场戏太棒了。

1112
00:55:25.290 --> 00:55:26.230
Such a good scene.
真是场好戏。

1113
00:55:26.410 --> 00:55:35.030
One thing about the scene that made it tricky that you might not think of is that this is one of the few times where Dwight and I have to be standing facing one another.
关于这场戏有个你可能想不到的难点，这是我和德怀特为数不多需要面对面站着的场景之一。

1114
00:55:35.690 --> 00:55:38.170
And you really see our height difference.
你能清楚地看到我们的身高差。

1115
00:55:38.710 --> 00:55:42.470
I knew it was a wide shot because it was a spy shot.
我知道那是广角镜头，因为那是偷拍视角。

1116
00:55:42.470 --> 00:55:46.870
But now it makes me think it was also that wide to fit you both in frame.
但现在我想，用那么广的镜头也是为了把你们俩都拍进画面里。

1117
00:55:46.870 --> 00:55:47.490
Yes.
没错。

1118
00:55:47.750 --> 00:55:55.770
And the other thing, the other thing to point out, which I thought was really great, is you can really see that Dwight is wearing a Cooper's seafood t-shirt.
还有一点，我觉得非常棒，值得一提的是，你能清楚地看到德怀特穿着一件库珀海鲜店的T恤。

1119
00:55:56.950 --> 00:55:57.470
Hey.
嘿。

1120
00:55:57.890 --> 00:55:58.150
Yeah.
没错。

1121
00:55:58.150 --> 00:55:59.890
A local Scranton reference there.
那是斯克兰顿当地的一个梗。

1122
00:56:00.150 --> 00:56:00.430
I know.
我知道。

1123
00:56:02.230 --> 00:56:05.390
Well, next up is the sumo competition.
好了，接下来是相扑比赛。

1124
00:56:05.770 --> 00:56:07.590
Oh, my goodness, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

1125
00:56:08.070 --> 00:56:09.070
Where to begin?
从何说起呢？

1126
00:56:09.330 --> 00:56:10.470
Where to begin?
从何说起呢？

1127
00:56:10.670 --> 00:56:11.470
Where to begin?
从何说起呢？

1128
00:56:11.690 --> 00:56:16.290
I'll tell you, I did one of those, like, a guffa.
我跟你说，我当时真的笑喷了。

1129
00:56:16.550 --> 00:56:17.190
Is that the word?
是这个词吗？

1130
00:56:17.290 --> 00:56:18.630
Where you laugh out loud?
就是那种大声笑出来？

1131
00:56:18.830 --> 00:56:19.310
Yeah.
没错。

1132
00:56:19.310 --> 00:56:22.390
Like, it takes over your body and you can't even suppress it?
就是那种笑到无法自控，甚至压抑不住？

1133
00:56:22.710 --> 00:56:32.010
When I saw John in his little toothpick legs walk out in that sumo suit, look at his legs.
当我看到约翰穿着相扑服，露出那双牙签腿走出来时，看看他的腿。

1134
00:56:32.010 --> 00:56:38.990
If you haven't, look at his tiny little legs sticking out of that sumo suit and his little head popping up.
如果你还没看过，去看看他那双从相扑服里伸出来的小细腿，还有他那颗探出来的小脑袋。

1135
00:56:38.990 --> 00:56:41.550
It made me laugh so hard.
真的把我笑死了。

1136
00:56:42.110 --> 00:56:47.810
Now, I know that those guys were just so hot in those suits.
我知道他们穿那些衣服肯定热坏了。

1137
00:56:47.810 --> 00:56:48.110
Oh, yeah.
噢，是啊。

1138
00:56:48.110 --> 00:56:49.250
They were dying.
他们都快热死了。

1139
00:56:49.510 --> 00:56:54.790
And we had these little fans that they would try to, like, cool them off with.
我们当时有那种小风扇，试图给他们降降温。

1140
00:56:54.890 --> 00:56:58.930
But I'm sure that they were just so sweaty.
但我敢肯定他们当时一定汗流浃背。

1141
00:56:59.710 --> 00:57:03.510
But they also had the best time in those.
不过他们穿上那身衣服也玩得最开心。

1142
00:57:03.630 --> 00:57:05.970
They were like, they all turned into children.
他们就像变成了小孩子一样。

1143
00:57:06.250 --> 00:57:09.510
And they were loving it, I have to say.
不得不说，他们玩得很尽兴。

1144
00:57:09.610 --> 00:57:14.830
They couldn't wait to run at each other and, like, throw themselves at each other and all of it.
他们迫不及待地冲向对方，把自己撞向对方，诸如此类。

1145
00:57:14.870 --> 00:57:16.010
They were having so much fun.
他们玩得太开心了。

1146
00:57:16.010 --> 00:57:20.850
But I do remember, between takes, they could not sit down.
但我记得在拍摄间隙，他们根本坐不下来。

1147
00:57:21.430 --> 00:57:21.870
Yes.
没错。

1148
00:57:22.170 --> 00:57:23.430
They could not sit down.
他们坐不下来。

1149
00:57:23.570 --> 00:57:27.530
And people would run over with, like, little umbrellas and these fans to try to cool them off.
大家会跑过去，拿着小伞和风扇试图给他们降温。

1150
00:57:27.770 --> 00:57:30.150
And Jenna, I was hanging out with Rain.
还有珍娜，我当时正和雷恩待在一起。

1151
00:57:30.270 --> 00:57:38.510
And I have this great photo that one of the things I loved is that I could lean on Rain's belly like I had something to prop myself up on.
我有一张很棒的照片，我最喜欢的一点是，我可以靠在雷恩的肚子上，就像有个东西能支撑我一样。

1152
00:57:38.510 --> 00:57:45.950
So I have this photo, and it's him and I casually talking, but I'm resting myself on his sumo belly.
所以我拍了这张照片，照片里我和他正在闲聊，但我整个人靠在他的相扑肚皮上。

1153
00:57:46.850 --> 00:57:47.990
That's incredible.
那太不可思议了。

1154
00:57:48.590 --> 00:57:53.670
Well, we had a fan question from Freya McKenzie and Jesse Magison.
嗯，我们收到了弗雷亚·麦肯齐和杰西·马吉森的粉丝提问。

1155
00:57:53.670 --> 00:58:01.230
Is it true that Rain Wilson actually put Leslie David Baker in the hospital while shooting beach games?
雷恩·威尔森在拍摄《海滩游戏》时真的把莱斯利·大卫·贝克送进医院了吗？

1156
00:58:01.630 --> 00:58:02.250
Yes.
是的。

1157
00:58:02.250 --> 00:58:02.630
Yes.
是的。

1158
00:58:03.270 --> 00:58:14.370
What happened was that during all this sumo wrestling, Leslie got sand in his eyes, and they tried to flush it out, but they couldn't.
当时的情况是，在相扑比赛中，莱斯利的眼睛进了沙子，他们试着冲洗，但没能洗出来。

1159
00:58:14.370 --> 00:58:23.270
And I remember he had to leave set, and I don't know if he went to the hospital or to an eye doctor, but he had a scratched cornea.
我记得他不得不离开片场，我不确定他是去了医院还是眼科医生那里，但他确实划伤了角膜。

1160
00:58:23.750 --> 00:58:23.910
Yeah.
没错。

1161
00:58:24.070 --> 00:58:28.530
I thought they took him to a local, like, the clinic, the nearest hospital.
我以为他们带他去了当地的诊所，就是最近的医院。

1162
00:58:28.770 --> 00:58:38.730
Every single day when you're filming, whether it's on set or location, they put in the call sheet the location where you're filming and the nearest hospital's location.
每天拍摄的时候，无论是在片场还是外景地，通告单上都会写明拍摄地点和最近的医院位置。

1163
00:58:39.310 --> 00:58:39.730
Yeah.
是的。

1164
00:58:39.910 --> 00:58:42.810
They researched that ahead of time for this reason.
他们提前研究过这些，就是为了以防万一。

1165
00:58:42.810 --> 00:58:46.890
So I think they took him to the nearest, whatever that was, clinic, right?
所以我认为他们带他去了最近的那个诊所，对吧？

1166
00:58:47.370 --> 00:58:47.750
Yeah.
没错。

1167
00:58:47.890 --> 00:58:51.310
And he was in quite a bit of pain, and he was like, no, it's still in there.
他当时非常痛苦，一直说，不，东西还在里面。

1168
00:58:51.390 --> 00:58:52.710
There's something wrong.
肯定有什么不对劲。

1169
00:58:52.930 --> 00:58:55.990
You know that moment in your body where you're like, it's not right.
你知道那种感觉，就是身体告诉你，这不对劲。

1170
00:58:56.030 --> 00:58:56.950
Something's not right.
有什么地方不对劲。

1171
00:58:57.290 --> 00:59:00.330
And it had, in fact, scratched his cornea.
事实上，他的角膜确实被划伤了。

1172
00:59:00.710 --> 00:59:05.190
And they treated him, and then he came back and finished filming because he's such a trooper.
他们给他处理了一下，然后他就回来完成了拍摄，他真是个硬汉。

1173
00:59:06.150 --> 00:59:08.370
Well, I've had this happen to me, Angela.
嗯，安吉拉，我也遇到过这种情况。

1174
00:59:08.370 --> 00:59:13.870
I got a piece of sand in my eye by using a face scrub.
我用磨砂膏洗脸时，沙子进了眼睛。

1175
00:59:14.010 --> 00:59:14.690
Oh, Lord.
天哪。

1176
00:59:15.050 --> 00:59:15.750
With sand in it.
里面有沙子的那种。

1177
00:59:17.130 --> 00:59:24.530
And I got a piece in my eye, and I was like, it feels like something's in your eye when you scratch your cornea.
有一粒进了我眼睛，那种感觉就像角膜划伤了一样，总觉得眼睛里有东西。

1178
00:59:24.550 --> 00:59:26.470
But I couldn't find it.
但我怎么也找不到它。

1179
00:59:26.470 --> 00:59:30.010
So I went to an eye doctor, and I had scratched my cornea.
所以我去看眼科医生，结果发现我的角膜被划伤了。

1180
00:59:30.330 --> 00:59:32.710
So I feel for Leslie.
所以我很同情莱斯利。

1181
00:59:32.710 --> 00:59:35.270
It is a very, it is a not fun feeling.
那真是一种非常、非常糟糕的感觉。

1182
00:59:35.570 --> 00:59:37.470
I have never scratched my cornea.
我从来没划伤过角膜。

1183
00:59:37.630 --> 00:59:42.730
But one time, I was eating jalapeno potato chips because I love them so much.
但有一次，我在吃墨西哥辣椒味的薯片，因为我太爱吃了。

1184
00:59:42.930 --> 00:59:45.650
And I bit into it kind of aggressively.
我咬得有点猛。

1185
00:59:45.870 --> 00:59:50.370
And the jalapeno dust off the chip went into my eyes.
薯片上的辣椒粉飞进了我的眼睛里。

1186
00:59:51.590 --> 00:59:53.570
And it was very painful.
那真的非常疼。

1187
00:59:54.010 --> 00:59:54.990
Why are you laughing?
你笑什么？

1188
00:59:55.430 --> 00:59:56.470
This really happened.
这是真的发生的。

1189
00:59:57.170 --> 00:59:58.610
I bit into the chip, and then I was like, ah!
我咬了一口薯片，然后就大叫，啊！

1190
01:00:02.860 --> 01:00:03.300
Laughing.
（笑声）

1191
01:00:04.020 --> 01:00:08.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

1192
01:00:09.030 --> 01:00:10.630
Okay, we should probably get back on topic.
好吧，我们还是回到正题吧。

1193
01:00:11.690 --> 01:00:12.130
Yeah.
好的。

1194
01:00:12.390 --> 01:00:13.510
Well, here's the thing.
是这样的。

1195
01:00:13.510 --> 01:00:20.630
I remember Leslie leaving set, but I don't remember when exactly it happened or how it happened.
我记得莱斯利离开了片场，但我不记得具体是什么时候发生的，也不记得是怎么发生的。

1196
01:00:20.650 --> 01:00:22.150
I just know he got sand in his eye.
我只知道他的眼睛进了沙子。

1197
01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:22.770
All right.
好吧。

1198
01:00:22.850 --> 01:00:23.870
This is what I think happened.
我是这么认为的。

1199
01:00:24.030 --> 01:00:25.610
I watched the deleted scenes.
我看了删减片段。

1200
01:00:25.810 --> 01:00:31.290
And there's a moment, it's not in the episode, where Dwight is wrestling with Stanley and
有一个片段，正片里没有，是德怀特和斯坦利摔跤的时候，然后

1201
01:00:31.290 --> 01:00:33.950
knocks him to the ground and is like, take that, old man.
把他打倒在地，还说，尝尝这个，老家伙。

1202
01:00:34.110 --> 01:00:36.730
And he kind of kicks at the sand, right?
然后他踢了踢沙子，对吧？

1203
01:00:37.430 --> 01:00:38.210
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1204
01:00:38.210 --> 01:00:39.170
I'm remembering this.
我想起来了。

1205
01:00:39.170 --> 01:00:39.290
Yes.
是的。

1206
01:00:39.370 --> 01:00:45.090
And I think then Rain felt really bad because he realized in that moment, that's when we
我觉得当时雷恩（Rainn）心里一定很不好受，因为他意识到那一刻，就是我们

1207
01:00:45.090 --> 01:00:45.710
thought it happened.
以为事情发生的时候。

1208
01:00:47.090 --> 01:00:47.630
Yes.
没错。

1209
01:00:48.010 --> 01:00:48.950
That's right.
就是这样。

1210
01:00:49.370 --> 01:00:49.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1211
01:00:49.870 --> 01:00:50.530
That's right.
没错。

1212
01:00:51.170 --> 01:00:55.090
Well, this was not the only injury from this episode.
好吧，这一集里受伤的不止他一个。

1213
01:00:56.450 --> 01:00:59.810
Ed hurt his finger during the sumo wrestling.
艾德（Ed）在相扑比赛时弄伤了手指。

1214
01:00:59.970 --> 01:01:00.390
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

1215
01:01:00.430 --> 01:01:02.570
I think he like lost a fingernail or something.
我想他好像是掉了指甲还是怎么的。

1216
01:01:03.130 --> 01:01:06.470
He was like, sorry, it makes me laugh so hard.
他当时说，抱歉，这让我笑得停不下来。

1217
01:01:06.670 --> 01:01:07.730
I shouldn't laugh.
我不该笑的。

1218
01:01:07.730 --> 01:01:12.970
But it's when that moment, if you guys watch it, when Andy and Dwight really start going
但那一刻，如果你们去重看的话，当安迪（Andy）和德怀特（Dwight）真的开始

1219
01:01:12.970 --> 01:01:16.130
at each other, like Dwight walks over and he's eating a sandwich, even though he's eating
互相攻击时，德怀特走过去，嘴里还吃着三明治，尽管他已经吃了

1220
01:01:16.130 --> 01:01:17.010
all these hot dogs.
那么多热狗了。

1221
01:01:17.210 --> 01:01:20.110
He walks over and then they just start going at each other.
他走过去，然后他们就开始扭打在一起。

1222
01:01:20.230 --> 01:01:22.310
And Ed is like kind of flailing his arms at him.
艾德当时就在那儿胡乱挥舞着手臂。

1223
01:01:22.850 --> 01:01:28.310
Somehow in this tussle, Ed broke his fingernail, but he said he broke it really bad.
在这次扭打中，艾德不知怎么就把指甲弄断了，他说断得非常严重。

1224
01:01:28.410 --> 01:01:29.050
Like it ripped.
就像撕裂了一样。

1225
01:01:29.050 --> 01:01:31.410
I think it like ripped below the...
我想是撕裂到了……下面。

1226
01:01:31.410 --> 01:01:32.130
That's what I...
我记得就是……

1227
01:01:32.130 --> 01:01:34.510
I remember like it was gruesome looking.
我记得看起来特别惨烈。

1228
01:01:34.510 --> 01:01:34.890
It was gruesome.
确实很惨烈。

1229
01:01:35.050 --> 01:01:37.750
But Ed was like yelling in his sumo suit.
但艾德穿着相扑服在那儿大喊大叫。

1230
01:01:37.890 --> 01:01:39.090
He was yelling, stop, stop.
他喊着，停下，停下。

1231
01:01:39.350 --> 01:01:42.310
And all he could get out was, I broke my nail.
他只能喊出，我指甲断了。

1232
01:01:42.310 --> 01:01:45.570
And people were like, okay, did you break your fingernail?
大家就说，好吧，你是弄断了指甲吗？

1233
01:01:45.890 --> 01:01:48.530
He's like, no, guys, I broke my nail.
他说，不，伙计们，我指甲断了。

1234
01:01:49.170 --> 01:01:50.070
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1235
01:01:50.930 --> 01:01:51.750
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1236
01:01:52.990 --> 01:01:54.270
But he didn't leave set.
但他没有离开片场。

1237
01:01:54.490 --> 01:01:55.450
No, he didn't leave set.
不，他没离开。

1238
01:01:55.590 --> 01:01:56.670
They came over and they...
他们走过去，然后他们……

1239
01:01:56.670 --> 01:01:59.210
But there was that moment when someone was like, what happened?
但当时有人问，发生什么事了？

1240
01:01:59.310 --> 01:02:00.330
Like Ed broke his nail.
就像是艾德指甲断了。

1241
01:02:00.450 --> 01:02:03.350
And he's like, no, it's more than just a broken nail.
他说，不，这不仅仅是断了个指甲那么简单。

1242
01:02:03.510 --> 01:02:05.210
And then they wrapped it up.
然后他们就把伤口包扎了一下。

1243
01:02:05.970 --> 01:02:10.550
Well, now, Angela, we're going to get into a big moment.
好了，安吉拉（Angela），我们要进入一个重大时刻了。

1244
01:02:10.910 --> 01:02:12.530
This was huge for our show.
这对我们的剧集来说意义重大。

1245
01:02:12.670 --> 01:02:13.810
This is a huge stunt.
这是一个巨大的特技场面。

1246
01:02:14.070 --> 01:02:18.750
You have to remember, our show never left a little tiny office.
你们得记住，我们的剧从来没离开过那个小小的办公室。

1247
01:02:18.930 --> 01:02:20.990
So we've got to break down.
所以我们得拆解一下。

1248
01:02:21.130 --> 01:02:22.430
We've got two big things coming up.
接下来有两件大事。

1249
01:02:22.430 --> 01:02:27.030
We've got this Andy floating away and then the coals.
一个是安迪飘走，另一个是煤炭火堆。

1250
01:02:27.330 --> 01:02:28.490
So Jenna, let's start with Andy.
那么珍娜（Jenna），我们先从安迪开始吧。

1251
01:02:29.250 --> 01:02:29.490
Okay.
好的。

1252
01:02:29.910 --> 01:02:32.210
Andy walks over to the water.
安迪走向水边。

1253
01:02:32.350 --> 01:02:37.110
And we had a fan question about this from Allie Jo Higginbotham, who said,
我们收到了一条来自艾莉·乔·希金博瑟姆的粉丝提问，她说，

1254
01:02:37.730 --> 01:02:40.770
when Andy walks to the lake, he has something yellow in his hand.
当安迪走向湖边时，他手里拿着一个黄色的东西。

1255
01:02:40.910 --> 01:02:41.650
What is he holding?
他拿的是什么？

1256
01:02:41.890 --> 01:02:44.350
And what is he planning to do with it at the shore?
他打算在岸边用它做什么？

1257
01:02:44.830 --> 01:02:47.910
Well, he's holding a...
嗯，他拿的是……

1258
01:02:47.910 --> 01:02:48.890
A bandana.
一条头巾。

1259
01:02:49.130 --> 01:02:50.490
He's holding a yellow bandana.
他拿的是一条黄色头巾。

1260
01:02:50.490 --> 01:02:53.190
Michael had handed these out in the egg race.
这是迈克尔在蛋赛中分发的。

1261
01:02:53.290 --> 01:02:56.350
And that's what everyone had used to cover their eyes.
每个人都用它来蒙住眼睛。

1262
01:02:56.510 --> 01:02:59.330
And Andy is holding his yellow bandana from the egg race.
安迪手里拿的就是他那条蛋赛用的黄色头巾。

1263
01:02:59.330 --> 01:03:00.370
And he's going to...
他打算……

1264
01:03:00.370 --> 01:03:04.790
He hopes to dip it in the water to then maybe wrap it around his neck to cool himself off.
他希望能把它浸在水里，然后围在脖子上给自己降降温。

1265
01:03:04.910 --> 01:03:05.770
This was the idea.
这就是他的想法。

1266
01:03:06.610 --> 01:03:06.970
Yes.
没错。

1267
01:03:07.130 --> 01:03:10.770
But instead, he falls in the water and starts floating away.
但结果他掉进了水里，开始漂走了。

1268
01:03:11.410 --> 01:03:15.970
When he fell in the water, you know, I wasn't too far off because my character witnesses this.
他掉进水里的时候，其实我离得不远，因为我的角色目睹了这一切。

1269
01:03:16.310 --> 01:03:16.790
Yes.
是的。

1270
01:03:16.790 --> 01:03:21.870
And there is a take that didn't make it that he literally went...
有一个没被剪进正片的镜头，他当时真的……

1271
01:03:21.870 --> 01:03:23.250
He like rolled, Jenna.
他就像滚进去的一样，珍娜。

1272
01:03:23.570 --> 01:03:26.090
He like rolled into the water.
他就像滚进了水里。

1273
01:03:26.430 --> 01:03:32.090
But they used this take because it was more clear why he was going down there.
但他们用了现在这个镜头，因为这样更清楚他为什么要下水。

1274
01:03:32.250 --> 01:03:36.090
He's trying to hang that bandana in the water, trying to balance.
他想把头巾浸在水里，试图保持平衡。

1275
01:03:36.910 --> 01:03:44.310
Well, let me say, and we got another frequently asked question from Candice Kelso, Michael Loong,
好吧，让我说一下，我们还收到了坎迪斯·凯尔索、迈克尔·隆、

1276
01:03:45.110 --> 01:03:47.610
Olive Taylor, and Phoebe Bono.
奥利夫·泰勒和菲比·博诺的常见问题。

1277
01:03:47.950 --> 01:03:51.630
Was that really Ed in the water or was that a stunt double?
在水里的真的是艾德本人，还是替身演员？

1278
01:03:51.870 --> 01:03:53.850
Guys, that was Ed in the water.
伙计们，在水里的就是艾德本人。

1279
01:03:54.110 --> 01:03:55.370
Ed did it all.
全都是艾德自己演的。

1280
01:03:55.570 --> 01:03:57.430
I don't know that they offered him a stunt double.
我不知道他们有没有给他提供替身。

1281
01:03:57.750 --> 01:03:58.390
I don't know.
我不知道。

1282
01:03:58.990 --> 01:04:01.230
Kent told me they offered him a stunt double,
肯特告诉我他们确实给他提供了替身，

1283
01:04:01.230 --> 01:04:05.350
but Ed insisted on doing all of the floating in the water himself.
但艾德坚持要自己完成所有的水上漂浮戏份。

1284
01:04:05.750 --> 01:04:10.710
He was out there floating for over 45 minutes.
他在水里漂了45分钟多。

1285
01:04:11.250 --> 01:04:17.370
And I'm thinking maybe when he was like, oh, no, I'll fall in the water.
我在想，也许当他说“哦，不，我会掉进水里”的时候，

1286
01:04:17.730 --> 01:04:21.410
Like, maybe he didn't realize what that all entailed.
他可能没意识到这到底意味着什么。

1287
01:04:21.870 --> 01:04:22.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1288
01:04:22.190 --> 01:04:28.750
And perhaps having a stunt double on the side to complete some of the very far away floating.
也许在旁边安排一个替身来完成一些远景的漂浮镜头会更好。

1289
01:04:29.070 --> 01:04:34.030
But guys, that is Ed the whole time floating out there.
但伙计们，在那儿漂着的全程都是艾德本人。

1290
01:04:34.210 --> 01:04:37.850
Not only in the day, but then he had to do it again at night.
不仅是白天，晚上他还得再拍一次。

1291
01:04:38.510 --> 01:04:42.210
This was two different shoots for him in the water.
对他来说，这是两次不同的水下拍摄。

1292
01:04:42.430 --> 01:04:44.210
A day scene and a night scene.
一场白天的戏和一场晚上的戏。

1293
01:04:44.770 --> 01:04:52.770
Now, when he was out there at night, he did have a thin wetsuit on underneath all that sumo gear to keep him warm.
不过，当他晚上在水里时，他在那身相扑装下面穿了一件薄潜水服来保暖。

1294
01:04:52.970 --> 01:04:54.150
So they did think of that.
所以他们还是考虑到了这一点。

1295
01:04:54.290 --> 01:05:00.710
But before we get too far into this stunt, Angela, we also had fan questions from Rebecca Gonzalez,
但在我们深入讨论这个特技之前，安吉拉，我们还收到了来自丽贝卡·冈萨雷斯、

1296
01:05:01.530 --> 01:05:04.250
Connor N, and Maura Anderson, who said,
康纳·N和莫拉·安德森的粉丝提问，他们说，

1297
01:05:04.490 --> 01:05:08.830
Angela, how did you make it through the scene of Andy floating away?
安吉拉，你是怎么忍住没在安迪漂走的戏份里笑场的？

1298
01:05:09.770 --> 01:05:11.210
It was so hard.
太难了。

1299
01:05:11.410 --> 01:05:12.730
It was, that's what she said.
确实，这就是她说的。

1300
01:05:13.650 --> 01:05:14.370
Oh, boy.
天哪。

1301
01:05:14.470 --> 01:05:14.930
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1302
01:05:15.470 --> 01:05:17.090
It was really, I'm sorry.
真的，我很抱歉。

1303
01:05:17.230 --> 01:05:18.250
It was really difficult.
那真的很难。

1304
01:05:19.270 --> 01:05:20.770
Difficult not to laugh.
很难不笑出来。

1305
01:05:21.210 --> 01:05:21.970
Really difficult.
真的很难。

1306
01:05:22.330 --> 01:05:25.710
Especially because Ed was improvising a little bit.
尤其是因为艾德当时即兴发挥了一点。

1307
01:05:25.830 --> 01:05:30.110
As he floated away, some of that dialogue was not scripted.
当他漂走的时候，有些台词并不是剧本里写的。

1308
01:05:30.270 --> 01:05:34.970
So, you know, when I'm like, I don't really understand what it is you're saying to me.
所以，你知道，当我说“我真的听不懂你在跟我说什么”的时候。

1309
01:05:35.150 --> 01:05:36.110
That was scripted.
那是剧本写的。

1310
01:05:36.230 --> 01:05:42.610
But then Ed, Ed was physically floating away and he was dealing with the elements and he improvised this line.
但后来艾德，艾德当时身体正在漂走，他还要应对各种环境因素，于是他即兴说了这句台词。

1311
01:05:42.730 --> 01:05:47.570
Look at what I'm doing and go tell somebody it.
看看我在做什么，然后去告诉别人。

1312
01:05:48.050 --> 01:05:50.190
I love that line so much.
我太喜欢那句台词了。

1313
01:05:50.390 --> 01:05:52.110
That was Ed improvising.
那是艾德即兴发挥的。

1314
01:05:52.790 --> 01:05:54.570
That is awesome.
那太棒了。

1315
01:05:54.790 --> 01:05:55.190
I know.
我知道。

1316
01:05:55.370 --> 01:05:56.330
So it was really hard.
所以这真的很难。

1317
01:05:56.430 --> 01:06:00.190
And I didn't want to laugh because poor Ed is floating out in that water.
我不想笑，因为可怜的艾德正漂在水里。

1318
01:06:00.330 --> 01:06:01.110
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1319
01:06:01.670 --> 01:06:04.730
Yes, if you laugh, you ruin that moment.
是的，如果你笑了，你就毁了那一刻。

1320
01:06:04.730 --> 01:06:05.110
Yes.
是的。

1321
01:06:05.210 --> 01:06:06.650
And he has to float longer.
而且他得漂更久。

1322
01:06:06.810 --> 01:06:07.650
I was working hard.
我当时很努力地忍着。

1323
01:06:07.650 --> 01:06:08.370
Oh, the pressure of that.
噢，那压力可真大。

1324
01:06:08.490 --> 01:06:09.430
I was working hard not to laugh.
我当时很努力地不让自己笑出来。

1325
01:06:10.310 --> 01:06:15.550
Well, we asked Jen about Ed in the water and here's what she had to say.
嗯，我们问了简关于艾德在水里的事，以下是她的说法。

1326
01:06:15.790 --> 01:06:19.110
Oh, shooting the Andy floating away scenes was really fun.
噢，拍摄安迪漂走的场景真的很有趣。

1327
01:06:19.310 --> 01:06:21.030
I love that part of the script.
我喜欢剧本里的那一部分。

1328
01:06:21.030 --> 01:06:27.230
I love when Angela pretends that she doesn't understand what he's saying.
我喜欢安吉拉假装听不懂他在说什么的那段。

1329
01:06:27.230 --> 01:06:28.550
That was so much fun to write.
写那段真的很有意思。

1330
01:06:30.090 --> 01:06:37.070
I remember that Ed was like in the sumo suit and then there was a rope attached to him and
我记得艾德当时穿着相扑服，身上系着一根绳子，然后

1331
01:06:37.070 --> 01:06:42.330
he was being pulled by a boat and then at a certain point the boat would leave him and
他被一艘船拉着，然后在某个时刻船会离开他，

1332
01:06:42.330 --> 01:06:43.530
then he would just drift.
然后他就只能随波逐流。

1333
01:06:43.770 --> 01:06:45.090
But there was also a current.
但当时还有水流。

1334
01:06:45.250 --> 01:06:49.910
I believe the water was also cold and he had to keep his head up.
我相信水也很冷，他必须保持头部露出水面。

1335
01:06:50.030 --> 01:06:54.490
And I remember that it was a challenging thing because his head would sort of get lost and
我记得那是一件很有挑战性的事情，因为他的头会有点沉下去，

1336
01:06:54.490 --> 01:06:56.890
it would just like go under unless he helped.
如果不帮忙的话，他就会沉下去。

1337
01:06:56.890 --> 01:07:00.470
He put his neck up and just try to hold it up.
他得伸长脖子，努力把头抬起来。

1338
01:07:00.550 --> 01:07:01.950
So I think it was a difficult thing.
所以我认为那是一件很困难的事情。

1339
01:07:01.950 --> 01:07:08.070
Also, the timing of the boat and the timing of us trying to get it on camera with Michael's
此外，船的时间安排，以及我们试图用摄像机捕捉到迈克尔

1340
01:07:08.070 --> 01:07:09.030
talking head was difficult.
访谈镜头的时机也很难把握。

1341
01:07:09.370 --> 01:07:14.530
So I remember that Ed was like a real trooper and there were a lot of discussions about
所以我记得艾德表现得非常坚强，我们当时讨论了很多次

1342
01:07:14.530 --> 01:07:17.690
like how far out he should be at sea because we wanted to see him.
关于他应该漂到离岸多远的地方，因为我们想拍到他。

1343
01:07:17.930 --> 01:07:21.870
We didn't want to be too obvious that it was him and Michael might see him, but we didn't
我们不想太明显地看出是他，也不想让迈克尔一眼就看到他，但我们也不

1344
